    <hasDescription>Turns each table reference of a clause into the Table with that name, creating it if missing; FROM, UPDATE and DELETE FROM clauses reference it (referencesTable), which makes it a ReferencedTable.</hasDescription>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.owl-ontologies.com/onDBTuning.owl#Rule"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.owl-ontologies.com/onDBTuning.owl#TableSubset">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Table Subset</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://www.owl-ontologies.com/onDBTuning.owl#TaskConcept"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Set of tables referenced by a basic query (TS in Agrawal et al., 2000, used by Weberling, section 3.1.1). Interesting when TS-Cost and TS-Weight reach the threshold C.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://www.owl-ontologies.com/onDBTuning.owl#Rule_MV_ExecutionBenefit">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.owl-ontologies.com/onDBTuning.owl#Rule"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <hasName>MV_ExecutionBenefit</hasName>
    <hasDescription>For each execution and each of its queries or subqueries compatible with a view, records a MaterializedViewBenefit HyGainVM = Cost(q) - HyCost(q) (Weberling, figure 17, lines 3-5).</hasDescription>
  </rdf:Description>
